rincipal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:88:| MC19 | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE with dated treatments, elections and transitions. U1, U3. | Define the supported treatment matrix, rule authority and version selection; show matched economic events under selected genuinely different treatments and identify unimplemented operations. | Partially repaired. Ch. 9 compares FIFO/LIFO/average and records dated rule selection. Selected IAS-equivalent paragraphs inspected in official AASB texts; US LIFO has company-policy evidence only, full ASC authority is blocked, and official ASBE version verification remains pending. Source dossiers record exact edition/period limits and correct Caterpillar inventories to Note 8. G7, G8, G13. The acquired panel now supplies report-level preparation-basis evidence across US GAAP, IFRS-oriented reporting and ASBE; this does not replace dated primary accounting authority. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:89:| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remain