{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#|G4|G7|G8|ASC|ASBE|revenue|tax|lease|foreign|compound'\"' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md && rg -n '\"'^(class |def )|compound|liability|interest|standard'\"' scripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py scripts/core_semantics.py scripts/check_accounting_p06.py && rg --files docs/design/research/standards docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers /home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:1:# Product-design gap audit\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:7:## Question, baseline and skeptical audit\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:21:Skeptical audit: assess the declared first release and later modules separately;\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:33:## Findings\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:47:### G1. Reconstruction defines the answer more precisely than the algorithm\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:73:### G2. The normative language and IR contracts remain incomplete\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:98:### G3. Ordinary disclosure uncertainty can leave the promised solver fragment\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:124:### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:133:and changes in equity. Consolidation, foreign-currency translation and\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:145:### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:164:### G6. Forward economic and probability models remain interfaces\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:192:### G7. Standards, banks and insurance are largely deferred requirements\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:199:paragraph-level rule implementations. US GAAP and ASBE acquisition/review are\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:218:### G8. Literature breadth exceeds the depth of the follow-up screening\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:246:### G9. Tool selection is a shortlist, without demonstrated adapter contracts\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:265:### G10. Acceptance and completion are not yet determinate\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:268:[unselected release criteria](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/10-validation.tex:100),\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:272:The real-company corpus, annotation/adjudication protocol and release-specific\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:285:release criteria and workload budgets before evaluation. Universal arbitrary\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:289:## Prioritised repair sequence\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:299:| 7 | Release-specific corpus/criteria, author review and later independent review | Separates a completed draft, a usable implementation and scientifically valid forecasts |\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:306:## Review evidence and limits\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:1:# Review against the AccDSL mission\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:9:## Answer and review scope\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:24:## Goals and current coverage\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:37:## Additional explicit findings\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:39:### G11. Whole-report coverage and narrative formalisation need a procedure\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:60:### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:62:Requirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:70:or two classifications of the same revenue that must not be summed together.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:79:### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:81:Requirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:98:### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:113:schema. A first release can explicitly support exogenous stress only without\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:119:### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:138:### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:156:### G17. Local evidence review needs a state machine and invalidation rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:174:### G18. Reproducibility needs identity and replay definitions, not only fields\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:193:## Completion consequences\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:213:## Evidence and limits of this pass\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:34:def digest(path: Path) -> str | None:\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:41:def unique_object(pairs):\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:50:def inventory(root: Path, relative: str) -> dict[str, str]:\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:64:def approval_reference(root: Path, relative: str) -> dict[str, str]:\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:83:def protection(root: Path, phase_inventory: str, execution_inventory: str) -> dict:\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:97:def finish_protection(root: Path, report: dict) -> dict:\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:105:def run_suite(module_name: str) -> dict:\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:117:def probes() -> list[dict]:\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:137:    query = {\"contract\":\"c\",\"context\":\"x\",\"evidence_view\":\"latest_available\",\"horizon\":\"1\",\"scenario\":\"base\",\"requested_outputs\":[\"interest\"],\"accrual_convention\":\"simple_actual_fraction\",\"group_by\":[\"rate\",\"maturity\",\"reset\",\"hedge\"]}\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:138:    observe(\"MC11\", lambda: resolve_bullet_debt(debt, query)[\"outputs\"][\"interest\"] == Fraction(17, 2))\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:139:    observe(\"APPROXIMATION\", lambda: (lambda x: x[\"approximation\"][\"bound\"] == \"3/2\")(resolve_bullet_debt(debt, query, approximation={\"target_rate\":\"0.06\",\"tolerance\":\"2\",\"error_bound\":\"3/2\",\"scope\":\"fixed_rate_interest\",\"evidence\":[\"probe\"]})))\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:151:def main(argv=None) -> int:\nscripts/check_accounting_p06.py:191:The tests independently verify 260 minus revised H1 110 equals H2 150 and reject subtraction using incompatible original H1 120. They reject parent/group, basis, measurement, currency, calendar, gross/net, overlap, omission, dangling/cyclic revision, future-information, unsupported treatment, unsupported scenario, stale-query, maturity-crossing, and missing-approximation-evidence cases. Historical byte availability marked unknown remains unresolved and is excluded from the integrated historical computation. Tests also mutate the selected H1 amount from 110 to 100: derived H2 changes from 150 to 160, and the synthetic debt interest changes from 7.5 to 8, while the preserved earlier result remains 150.\nscripts/core_semantics.py:17:class Invalid(Exception):\nscripts/core_semantics.py:23:def require(condition, code, location, detail):\nscripts/core_semantics.py:28:def strict_json(text):\nscripts/core_semantics.py:40:def rational(value, location):\nscripts/core_semantics.py:49:def iso_date(value, location):\nscripts/core_semantics.py:58:def instant(value, location):\nscripts/core_semantics.py:74:class Validator:\nscripts/core_semantics.py:346:                        'InterestExpense': ('Expense', 'interest'), 'Retained': ('Equity', 'retained')}\nscripts/core_semantics.py:479:            require(r['closing_policy'] == 'DemoDebt@1/close' and r['cash_flow_policy'] == 'DemoDebt@1/interest_operating'\nscripts/core_semantics.py:500:def validate(document, registry, schema, root):\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:18:def main():\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:47:    liability = Q(5)/Q('1.1') + Q(105)/Q('1.21')\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:48:    equity = 100-liability\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:49:    check('bond_issue_components', (liability, equity) == (Q(11050,121), Q(1050,121)))\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:51:    post(book, rows, 'issue', cash=100, liability=-liability, conversion_equity=-equity)\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:53:        expense = -book['liability'] * Q(1, 10)\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:54:        post(book, rows, f'interest_{period}', interest_expense=expense, liability=-expense)\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:55:        post(book, rows, f'coupon_{period}', liability=5, cash=-5)\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:56:        check(f'carrying_after_coupon_{period}', -book['liability'] == [Q(1050,11), Q(100)][period-1])\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:57:    check('coupon_and_discount_accretion', book['interest_expense'] == Q(2260,121))\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:60:    post(redeemed, redemption_rows, 'redemption_at_maturity', liability=100, cash=-100)\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:61:    post(converted, conversion_rows, 'conversion_at_maturity', liability=100, issued_share_equity=-100)\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:62:    check('bond_settlement_paths', redeemed['liability'] == converted['liability'] == 0 and\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:66:    values['bond'] = dict(issue_liability=str(liability), issue_equity=str(equity),\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:67:                          total_interest_expense=str(book['interest_expense']))\nscripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py:96:    sources = [ROOT/'docs/design/research/standards-support.json', Path(__file__)]\ndocs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/inventory.md\ndocs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/compound-bond.md\ndocs/design/research/standards/xbrl-oim.html\ndocs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/insurance.md\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/global-scientific-coding-agent-policy.md\ndocs/design/research/standards/ias32.html\ndocs/design/research/standards/ias32.txt\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/scholarly-literature-audit-policy.md\n/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/humanizer-ai-writing-patterns.md\ndocs/design/research/standards/aasb17.txt\ndocs/design/research/standards/temporal2018.pdf\ndocs/design/research/standards/aasb17.pdf\ndocs/design/research/standards/ifrs18.html\ndocs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt\ndocs/design/research/standards/caterpillar2024.txt\ndocs/design/research/standards/aasb102.pdf\ndocs/design/research/standards/ifrs17.html\ndocs/design/research/standards/asbe-reproduction.html\ndocs/design/research/standards/ifrs9.txt\ndocs/design/research/standards/caterpillar2024.pdf\ndocs/design/research/standards/ifrs18.txt\ndocs/design/research/standards/xbrl-oim.txt\ndocs/design/research/standards/aasb132.pdf\ndocs/design/research/standards/ifrs17.txt\ndocs/design/research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex\ndocs/design/research/standards/aasb102.txt\ndocs/design/research/standards/ifrs9.html\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor name in ['MISSION_CONTROL.md','docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md','docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md']:\n p=Path(name);print('\\\\n'+name);lines=p.read_text().splitlines();print('\\\\n'.join(lines[:24]))\np=Path('docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md');print('\\\\nRequirement rows');print('\\\\n'.join(l for l in p.read_text().splitlines() if any('| '+x+' |' in l for x in ['MC06','MC15','MC17','MC19','MC29','MC30'])))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor name in ['MISSION_CONTROL.md','docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md','docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md']:\n p=Path(name);print('\\\\n'+name);lines=p.read_text().splitlines();print('\\\\n'.join(lines[:24]))\np=Path('docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md');print('\\\\nRequirement rows');print('\\\\n'.join(l for l in p.read_text().splitlines() if any('| '+x+' |' in l for x in ['MC06','MC15','MC17','MC19','MC29','MC30'])))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\nMISSION_CONTROL.md\n# AccDSL mission control\n\nEstablished 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong) at the user's request.\nStatus: active mission; Version 1.2 is a repaired design candidate with checked\nreference cases. Full product, domain and human acceptance remain pending.\n\n## Purpose\n\nDesign a system that represents a company's historical financial disclosures,\npreserves economically different histories and interpretations compatible with\nthe evidence, and carries those alternatives into scenario-dependent future\njournals and financial statements. Preserve their separate conditional outcome\ndistributions or feasible sets, including uncertainty that cannot be assigned\ndefensible probabilities.\n\nThe immediate deliverable is a detailed, readable LaTeX product and method\ndesign, with compiled PDF, supporting literature and software investigation,\nprecise implementation contracts and acceptance examples. The eventual product\nis the working representation and simulation engine. A document build, a small\nfinancing example and an implemented prototype are different achievements.\n\n## Authority and origin\n\nThis mission records the user's existing directions; it does not replace new\n\ndocs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md\n# Accounting master checkpoint\n\nUpdated 3 October 2026, Hong Kong, during run `20261002T233421-cea9e631`.\nThe user's create/review/execute instruction and original standing grant remain\nactive. The catalog preserves all MC01–MC35 and G1–G18, with no missing IDs.\n\n## Active run and next action\n\nTool session `78463` is running. P00–P04 are accepted internally; P05 is\nplanning. Do not launch another master or edit controller files while it is\nactive. Poll the session and consult current state before resuming. This is\na dated checkpoint; saved state and events record subsequent changes.\n\n```text\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py status\n```\n\nAfter this invocation exits, resume with:\n\n```text\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py run\n```\n\nThe current invocation has the configured 7,200-second wall limit, sequential\n\ndocs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md\n# Active checkpoint\n\nUpdated: 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong), after multi-year source-corpus\nacceptance following the expanded-audit repair. The user directed us to do all\nfeasible internal work before costly professional review. MC35 preserves that work order.\nThe wider mission remains active; human review is not the next automatic step.\n\n## Accepted source corpus and next execution\n\nThe user's corpus-first work unit is complete at the source-acquisition layer:\n**192 of 192 target reports, 2018–2025, across nine issuers and three evidenced\naccounting families. All nine have eight consecutive complete years.**\n`target-panel-v2.json` is active and is now the collector's explicit default.\nHenkel replaces Unilever and Munich Re replaces Allianz under the reviewed\nsource-access repair; frozen v1 coverage and all original files remain under\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/snapshots/`.\n\nResume from the [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/index.html`, `coverage.json` and\n`integrity-manifest.json`. QA 6 revalidated all 244 retained original versions;\nthe independent hash/provenance/grid/PDF checks pass, and 20 regression tests\npass. The old 12-, 157- and 159-report counts are historical. There are 738\nattempt/revalidation records, not 738 benchmark observations.\n\n\nRequirement rows\n| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\n| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\n| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\n| MC19 | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE with dated treatments, elections and transitions. U1, U3. | Define the supported treatment matrix, rule authority and version selection; show matched economic events under selected genuinely different treatments and identify unimplemented operations. | Partially repaired. Ch. 9 compares FIFO/LIFO/average and records dated rule selection. Selected IAS-equivalent paragraphs inspected in official AASB texts; US LIFO has company-policy evidence only, full ASC authority is blocked, and official ASBE version verification remains pending. Source dossiers record exact edition/period limits and correct Caterpillar inventories to Note 8. G7, G8, G13. The acquired panel now supplies report-level preparation-basis evidence across US GAAP, IFRS-oriented reporting and ASBE; this does not replace dated primary accounting authority. |\n| MC29 | Conduct a broad, technically grounded literature survey beyond the original collection. U3, P. | Inspect relevant primary methods/theory/evaluation/appendices and official code where available; compare direct alternatives; make genuine backward/forward screening, source-specific omissions, corrections and claim support inspectable. | Partially repaired: 179 individual title/metadata decisions across 194 occurrences/72 searches replace generic exclusions; generation rejects unscreened candidates. Mack and selected rule sources add inspected technical support. All-candidate full-text review and later module literature are not complete. G8. |\n| MC30 | Preserve the relevant source library and precise provenance. U3, P. | Archive accessible relevant papers under the required naming convention, retain exact versions/anchors, preserve original files, and document unavailable sources without relying on their uninspected claims. | 32 catalogued paper PDFs verified by hash/page count, with original collection preserved; Apple filings and selected standards archived separately. Version/authority limits and four blocked papers remain recorded. Mechanical integrity does not certify every technical claim. G8. The additional financial-report corpus preserves 244 original versions, source/index/discovery hashes and an append-only attempt history; 192 target slots pass source acceptance. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The required P08 files are absent, and neither prior attempt has a structured plan response. The existing compound-bond dossier provides a useful starting point: it cites primary authority for classification and maturity conversion, but explicitly leaves subsequent measurement unverified. I’ll make that distinction central to the plan and retain the ASC/ASBE access gaps.\n"}}
