{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '124,144p;192,245p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md && sed -n '1,115p' scripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py && sed -n '1,50p' tests/test_accounting_p06.py\"","aggregated_output":"### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\n\nEvidence: [initial corporate scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/08-modules.tex:41)\nand [report production](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:209).\n\nSales, inventory, payroll, fixed assets and working capital are named, but\nrecognition, measurement and transition rules are not supplied as a coherent\nreference package. There is no complete company example joining accruals,\nsettlements, cost of sales, depreciation, closing, cash-flow classification\nand changes in equity. Consolidation, foreign-currency translation and\nrestatement have sound stated requirements but lack equivalent numerical\nspecifications. The tests for these operations mostly describe desired\nproperties without complete inputs and expected outputs.\n\nRequired repair: provide one deliberately bounded corporate profile with an\nopening state, event schedules, journal templates and all statement mappings.\nCarry it across annual and interim periods, including a correction and one\nperimeter or currency case. Every supported operation needs its assumptions,\npreconditions, state changes and expected reports; explicit exclusions are\nacceptable. A balanced financing illustration does not specify this package.\n\n### G7. Standards, banks and insurance are largely deferred requirements\n\nEvidence: [standards sources and limits](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/08-modules.tex:14),\n[banking](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/08-modules.tex:128),\nand [insurance](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/08-modules.tex:170).\n\nThe design explicitly relies on IFRS overview material rather than\nparagraph-level rule implementations. US GAAP and ASBE acquisition/review are\nfuture tasks. There is no matched economic-event example showing actual\ndifferences between the three reporting bases. Banking has an illustrative\none-horizon credit-loss calculation, but no specified allowance lifecycle or\nprudential-capital computation. Insurance names groups, cash flows, risk\nadjustments, service and finance effects without a complete cohort state and\nroll-forward. Hybrid instruments are described but not worked through competing\nsupported treatments.\n\nDeferring execution is reasonable. It means the document currently governs\nrequirements for those modules, not their implementation. Their claimed\ninfluence on the core representation also needs structural fixtures now, so\nthe types are tested before the later engines are built.\n\nRequired repair: define operation-level scope and primary authority for the\nfirst supported treatments. Add matched cross-standard examples and bank,\ninsurance and hybrid-instrument record/transition examples. Expand actuarial,\nregulatory and accounting literature alongside each method specification.\n\n### G8. Literature breadth exceeds the depth of the follow-up screening\n\nEvidence: [stated research scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/12-research.tex:76),\n[forward ledger](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/research/forward-snowball.json),\nand [ledger generator](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/build_design_research.py:182).\n\nThe 31 archived PDFs provide a broad starting point and important access gaps\nare honestly recorded. Nevertheless, 62 forward-search records contain 164\ncandidate records, of which 159 have the same generic disposition: outside\nthe core or a specialised extension, screened as metadata. The generator\nassigns that disposition by default and uses a few title-string exceptions.\nThese records do not establish 159 individually justified relevance decisions.\nFor example, a provenance-in-databases survey receives the blanket disposition\nalthough provenance is part of the proposed core. This does not establish that\nthe paper must be adopted; it does require a substantive exclusion rationale.\n\nThe four inaccessible sources are only one part of the gap. Accounting\nmeasurement, actuarial methods and some direct reconstruction/uncertainty\napproaches are expressly deferred. The current records therefore do not\nestablish a sufficiently deep survey for the entire requested implementation\nscope. They do not invalidate the individually supported claims already made.\n\nRequired repair: record actual screening decisions for relevant candidates;\nuse an unreviewed status until a decision exists. Inspect direct competitors,\nextensions, corrections and negative findings, expanding each implementation\nmethod's supporting literature. Do not treat the mere existence of six JSON\nledgers as evidence that the literature policy has been satisfied.\n\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Exact calculations and balanced journals for the three preparation dossiers.\n\nThese are authored examples and counterexamples, not accounting eligibility\ndecisions or a general accounting engine.\n\"\"\"\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom fractions import Fraction as Q\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport time\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\n\n\ndef main():\n    start = time.monotonic()\n    checks, journals, values = [], {}, {}\n\n    def check(name, condition):\n        if not condition:\n            raise AssertionError(name)\n        checks.append(dict(name=name, passed=True))\n\n    def post(book, entries, name, **amounts):\n        amounts = {k: Q(v) for k, v in amounts.items()}\n        if sum(amounts.values()) != 0:\n            raise AssertionError(f'Unbalanced journal: {name}')\n        for account, value in amounts.items():\n            book[account] += value\n        entries.append(dict(operation=name, debit_positive={k: str(v) for k, v in amounts.items()}))\n\n    # The same 20 physical units, followed by one sale of 12, under three rules.\n    costs = {'FIFO': Q(10)*5 + Q(2)*7, 'LIFO': Q(10)*7 + Q(2)*5, 'average': Q(12)*Q(120, 20)}\n    expected = {'FIFO': (64, 56), 'LIFO': (80, 40), 'average': (72, 48)}\n    for method, cost in costs.items():\n        check('cost_and_stock_' + method, (cost, 120-cost) == expected[method])\n    impaired = min(Q(56), Q(50))\n    recovered = min(Q(56), Q(54))\n    check('impairment_then_partial_reversal', (56-impaired, recovered-impaired, recovered) == (6, 4, 54))\n    check('reversal_capped_at_original_cost', min(Q(56), Q(60))-impaired == 6)\n    values['inventory'] = dict(costs={k: str(v) for k, v in costs.items()},\n                               original_cost='56', impaired='50', recovered='54', capped_recovery='56')\n\n    liability = Q(5)/Q('1.1') + Q(105)/Q('1.21')\n    equity = 100-liability\n    check('bond_issue_components', (liability, equity) == (Q(11050,121), Q(1050,121)))\n    book, rows = defaultdict(Q), []\n    post(book, rows, 'issue', cash=100, liability=-liability, conversion_equity=-equity)\n    for period in [1, 2]:\n        expense = -book['liability'] * Q(1, 10)\n        post(book, rows, f'interest_{period}', interest_expense=expense, liability=-expense)\n        post(book, rows, f'coupon_{period}', liability=5, cash=-5)\n        check(f'carrying_after_coupon_{period}', -book['liability'] == [Q(1050,11), Q(100)][period-1])\n    check('coupon_and_discount_accretion', book['interest_expense'] == Q(2260,121))\n    redeemed, converted = book.copy(), book.copy()\n    redemption_rows, conversion_rows = list(rows), list(rows)\n    post(redeemed, redemption_rows, 'redemption_at_maturity', liability=100, cash=-100)\n    post(converted, conversion_rows, 'conversion_at_maturity', liability=100, issued_share_equity=-100)\n    check('bond_settlement_paths', redeemed['liability'] == converted['liability'] == 0 and\n          converted['cash'] == 90 and converted['conversion_equity'] == -equity)\n    check('coupon_equals_yield_boundary', Q(5)/Q('1.05')+Q(105)/Q('1.1025') == 100)\n    journals['bond_redemption'], journals['bond_conversion'] = redemption_rows, conversion_rows\n    values['bond'] = dict(issue_liability=str(liability), issue_equity=str(equity),\n                          total_interest_expense=str(book['interest_expense']))\n\n    # Independent risk-transfer/non-performance inputs demonstrate why ceded\n    # claims state must not be computed by halving every gross balance.\n    for name, ceded_ra, nonperformance, expected in [\n        ('base', Q(1), Q(0), (Q(119), Q(72), Q(47), Q(27), Q(6))),\n        ('separate_transferred_risk', Q('1.5'), Q(0), (Q('119.5'), Q(72), Q('47.5'), Q('27.5'), Q('6.5'))),\n        ('nonperformance_loss', Q(1), Q(2), (Q(117), Q(72), Q(45), Q(25), Q(4)))]:\n        b, rows = defaultdict(Q), []\n        post(b, rows, 'capital', cash=20, capital=-20)\n        post(b, rows, 'premium_received', cash=120, remaining_coverage=-120)\n        post(b, rows, 'reinsurance_premium_paid', reinsurance_coverage=24, cash=-24)\n        post(b, rows, 'half_gross_service', remaining_coverage=60, revenue=-60)\n        post(b, rows, 'half_ceded_service', reinsurance_expense=12, reinsurance_coverage=-12)\n        post(b, rows, 'incurred_claims_and_risk', claims_expense=42, incurred_claims=-42)\n        post(b, rows, 'claims_paid', incurred_claims=30, cash=-30)\n        recovery = Q(40)*Q(1,2)+ceded_ra-nonperformance\n        post(b, rows, 'recognise_recovery', reinsurance_claims=recovery, recovery_income=-recovery)\n        post(b, rows, 'recovery_received', cash=15, reinsurance_claims=-15)\n        profit = -sum(b[a] for a in ['revenue', 'reinsurance_expense', 'claims_expense', 'recovery_income'])\n        assets = sum(b[a] for a in ['cash', 'reinsurance_coverage', 'reinsurance_claims'])\n        liabilities = -sum(b[a] for a in ['remaining_coverage', 'incurred_claims'])\n        eq = -b['capital']+profit\n        check('insurance_' + name, (assets, liabilities, eq, profit, b['reinsurance_claims']) == expected)\n        check('insurance_balance_' + name, assets == liabilities+eq and b['cash'] == 101)\n        journals['insurance_' + name] = rows\n        values['insurance_' + name] = {k: str(v) for k, v in dict(assets=assets, liabilities=liabilities,\n            equity=eq, profit=profit, cash=b['cash'], recovery_asset=b['reinsurance_claims']).items()}\n\n    sources = [ROOT/'docs/design/research/standards-support.json', Path(__file__)]\n    report = dict(status='passed', count=len(checks), checks=checks, calculations=values, journals=journals,\n                  command='python3 scripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py',\n                  timestamp_utc=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(), wall_seconds=time.monotonic()-start,\n                  sha256={str(p.relative_to(ROOT)): hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in sources},\n                  scope='Exact arithmetic and signed journal reconciliation under stated dossier assumptions; no source applicability or professional assurance verdict.')\n    out = ROOT/'docs/design/review/accounting-dossier-checks.json'\n    out.write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2)+'\\n')\n    print(json.dumps({k: report[k] for k in ['status', 'count', 'wall_seconds']}))\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n\"\"\"Deterministic P06 conformance tests with independent arithmetic/set oracles.\"\"\"\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport copy\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport unittest\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"scripts\"))\nfrom context_chronology_v1 import (  # noqa: E402\n    Context, DebtConstituent, MappingRule, P06Engine, P06Error,\n    map_components, combine_partitions, adapt_core_context, adapt_p03_reading, adapt_p01_source,\n    admit_uncertainty, check_partition, compatible_context, guard_information_view,\n    interest_certificate, resolve_bullet_debt, select_evidence, subtract_cumulative,\n)\n\n\ndef ctx(**overrides):\n    row = {\n        \"concept\": \"revenue\", \"entity\": \"Acme\", \"perimeter\": \"Acme\", \"perimeter_version\": \"2026\",\n        \"basis\": \"GAAP\", \"measurement\": \"historical_cost\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"currency\": \"USD\",\n        \"calendar\": \"gregorian\", \"dimensions\": {\"segment\": \"retail\"}, \"gross_net\": \"gross\",\n    }\n    row.update(overrides)\n    return Context.from_dict(row)\n\n\ndef assertions():\n    return [\n        {\"id\": \"h1-original\", \"concept\": \"sales\", \"value\": \"120\", \"period\": {\"start\": \"2025-01-01\", \"end\": \"2025-06-30\"}, \"available\": \"2025-08-01\", \"ingested\": \"2025-08-02\", \"supersedes\": [], \"source\": \"fixture:original\", \"historical_byte_vintage\": \"unknown\"},\n        {\"id\": \"h1-revised\", \"concept\": \"sales\", \"value\": \"110\", \"period\": {\"start\": \"2025-01-01\", \"end\": \"2025-06-30\"}, \"available\": \"2026-02-01\", \"ingested\": \"2026-02-02\", \"supersedes\": [\"h1-original\"], \"source\": \"fixture:revision\", \"historical_byte_vintage\": \"unknown\"},\n        {\"id\": \"fy25\", \"concept\": \"sales\", \"value\": \"260\", \"period\": {\"start\": \"2025-01-01\", \"end\": \"2025-12-31\"}, \"available\": \"2026-02-01\", \"ingested\": \"2026-02-02\", \"supersedes\": [], \"source\": \"fixture:annual\", \"historical_byte_vintage\": \"unknown\"},\n    ]\n\n\nclass ContextPartitionTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_equivalent_context_mapping_and_spelling_preserved(self):\n        source, target = ctx(concept=\"sales\", scale=\"thousands\", sign=\"credit\", precision=2), ctx(concept=\"revenue\", scale=\"thousands\", sign=\"credit\", precision=2)\n        rule = MappingRule(\"sales\", \"revenue\", provenance=(\"fixture:review\",))\n        witness = compatible_context(source, target, [rule], at=\"2026-01-01\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\"kind\"], \"equivalent\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\"source\"][\"concept\"], \"sales\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\"target\"][\"concept\"], \"revenue\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\"source\"][\"scale\"], \"thousands\")\n        self.assertEqual(witness[\"source\"][\"precision\"], 2)\n\n    def test_context_rejects_parent_basis_measurement_currency_calendar_gross_net(self):\n        for field, a, b, code in [\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
