s_allowed\": [\"Accounting dynamics and behavioural/econometric relationships can be joined in company simulation.\"], \"claims_forbidden\": [\"Tax-data starting point and funds formulation do not supply generic modern disclosure extraction or cash-flow semantics.\"], \"reading_scope\": \"Only the specified technical and comparison portions; no independent replication\", \"publication_status\": \"working/thesis/preprint version identified in catalogue\", \"correction_check\": {\"openalex_is_retracted\": \"not available\", \"crossref_notice_relations\": \"not available\", \"date\": \"2026-10-02\", \"interpretation\": \"No adverse notice found in checked metadata; not a comprehensive certification. Version discrepancies recorded separately.\"}, \"quarantine_status\": \"not quarantined; version qualifications retained\"}\ndocs/design/research/claim-support.json ['date', 'records']\n{\"claim\": \"ACTUS separates contract events/state/payoff and externally supplied risk factors\", \"class\": \"IMPLEMENTATION_EVIDENCE\", \"anchor\": \"research/standards/actus-techspecs.tex event/state/payoff and risk-factor interface\", \"limit\": \"Source inspection, not integration execution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Accounting movement dynamics can be linked to explicit behaviour\", \"class\": \"PRIMARY_TECHNICAL_SUPPORT\", \"sources\": [\"shahnazarian2004\", \"pierson2020\", \"halaj2016\", \"behn2019\"], \"anchor\": \"03-literature.tex cited model sections\", \"limit\": \"No parameter transfer or forecast superiority\"}\ndocs/design/research/catalog.json list\n{\"id\": \"shahnazarian2004\", \"title\": \"A Dynamic Microeconometric Simulation Model for Incorporated Businesses\", \"authors\": [\"Hovick Shahnazarian\"], \"first_author_surname\": \"Shahnazarian\", \"year\": 2004, \"local_path\": \"docs/papers/A Dynamic Microeconometric Simulation Model for Incorporated Businesses Shahnazarian (2004).pdf\", \"original_path\": \"docs/ML for accounting and management/A Dynamic Microeconometric Simulation Model for Incorporated Businesses Shahnazarian(04).pdf\", \"status\": \"verified PDF archived; targeted technical review recorded in source-support.json\", \"sha256\": \"1c6f5fbdbf1bf2f623bb445e62d4263df8997436d009da52cc8e469708d8e04d\", \"text_path\": \"docs/design/research/text/shahnazarian2004.txt\", \"pages\": 281}\ndocs/design/research/standards/ifrs9.txt characters 21887 IFRS - IFRS 9 Financial Instruments\nSkip to content\nSign in or register\nUpdate to our sign-in process\nPhrase search\nWord search\nABOUT US\nThe IFRS Foundation is a not-for-profit, public interest organisation established to develop high-quality, understandable, enforceable and globally accepted accounting and sustainability disclosure standards.\nOur Standards are developed by our two standard-setting boards, the International Accounting Standards B\ndocs/design/research/standards/ias32.txt characters 14058 IFRS - IAS 32 Financial Instruments: Presentation\nSkip to content\nSign in or register\nUpdate to our sign-in process\nPhrase search\nWord search\nABOUT US\nThe IFRS Foundation is a not-for-profit, public interest organisation established to develop high-quality, understandable, enforceable and globally accepted accounting and sustainability disclosure standards.\nOur Standards are developed by our two standard-setting boards, the International Accounti\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor n in ['scripts/core0_ir_v1.py','scripts/context_chronology_v1.py']:\n p=Path(n);print(n);print('\\\\n'.join(l for l in p.read_text().splitlines() if l.startswith(('class ','def ')))[:2300])\np=Path('data/accounting-master/next-plan.md');print('next-plan',p.read_text()[:600])\np=Path('scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text()); seq=d if isinstance(d,list) else d.get('phases',[]);print('P08 catalog',json.dumps(next((x for x in seq if x.get('id')=='P08'),None)))\np=Path('/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/scholarly-literature-audit-policy.md');print('literature policy',p.read_text()[:1900])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt');ls=p.read_text().splitlines()\nfor term in ['before 1 July 2026','28       ','31       ','AG31','AG32']:\n hit=next((i for i,l in enumerate(ls) if term in l and i>50),None)\n print(term,hit+1 if hit is not None else 'not matched')\n if hit is not None:print('\\\\n'.join(ls[max(0,hit-1):hit+9]))\np=Path('scripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py');print('\\\\nChecker bond implementation');print('\\\\n'.join(p.read_text().splitlines()[9:20]+p.read_text().splitlines()[44:68]))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt');ls=p.read_text().splitlines()\nfor term in ['before 1 July 2026','28       ','31       ','AG31','AG32']:\n hit=next((i for i,l in enumerate(ls) if term in l and i>50),None)\n print(term,hit+1 if hit is not None else 'not matched')\n if hit is not None:print('\\\\n'.join(ls[max(0,hit-1):hit+9]))\np=Path('scripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py');print('\\\\nChecker bond implementation');print('\\\\n'.join(p.read_text().splitlines()[9:20]+p.read_text().splitlines()[44:68]))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"before 1 July 2026 2720\nCompilation details are not part of AASB 132.\nThis compiled Standard applies to annual periods beginning on or after 1 January 2023 but before 1 July 2026. It\ntakes into account amendments up to and including 15 December 2022 and was prepared on 6 April 2023 by the staff\nof the Australian Accounting Standards Board (AASB).\nThis compilation is not a separate Accounting Standard made by the AASB. Instead, it is a representation of\nAASB 132 (August 2015) as amended by other Accounting Standards, which are listed in the table below.\n\n\nTable of Standards\nStandard          Date made           FRL identifier         Commence-           Effective date                         Application,\n28        1552\n\nAASB 132-compiled                                      28                               EXAMPLES\n                              Authorised Version F2023C00406 registered 04/05/2023\n\nIllustrative examples\nThese examples accompany, but are not part of, AASB 132.\n\n\nAccounting for contracts on equity instruments of an entity\nIE1          The following examples4 illustrate the application of paragraphs 15–27 and AASB 9 to the accounting for\n31        1732\n\nAASB 132-compiled                                          31                                              EXAMPLES\n                                  Authorised Version F2023C00406 registered 04/05/2023\n\n        (a) Cash for cash (‘net cash settlement’)\nIE8     On 1 February 20X2, Entity A enters into a contract with Entity B to pay the fair value of 1,000 of Entity\n        A’s own outstanding ordinary shares as of 31 January 20X3 in exchange for CU104,000 in cash (ie CU104\n        per share) on 31 January 20X3. The contract will be settled net in cash. Entity A records the following\n        journal entries.\n\nAG31 1385\n          holder’s perspective.\nAG31      A common form of compound financial instrument is a debt instrument with an embedded conversion\n          option, such as a bond convertible into ordinary shares of the issuer, and without any other embedded\n          derivative features. Paragraph 28 requires the issuer of such a financial instrument to present the liability\n          component and the equity component separately in the statement of financial position, as follows:\n          (a)       The issuer’s obligation to make scheduled payments of interest and principal is a financial\n                    liability that exists as long as the instrument is not converted. On initial recognition, the fair value\n                    of the liability component is the present value of the contractually determined stream of future\n                    cash flows discounted at the rate of interest applied at that time by the market to instruments of\n                    comparable credit status and providing substantially the same cash flows, on the same terms, but\nAG32 1397\n                    option has value on initial recognition even when it is out of the money.\nAG32      On conversion of a convertible instrument at maturity, the entity derecognises the liability component and\n          recognises it as equity. The original equity component remains as equity (although it may be transferred\n          from one line item within equity to another). There is no gain or loss on conversion at maturity.\nAG33      When an entity extinguishes a convertible instrument before maturity through an early redemption or\n          repurchase in which the original conversion privileges are unchanged, the entity allocates the consideration\n          paid and any transaction costs for the repurchase or redemption to the liability and equity components of the\n          instrument at the date of the transaction. The method used in allocating the consideration paid and\n          transaction costs to the separate components is consistent with that used in the original allocation to the\n          separate components of the proceeds received by the entity when the convertible instrument was issued, in\n\nChecker bond implementation\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport time\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\n\n\ndef main():\n    start = time.monotonic()\n    checks, journals, values = [], {}, {}\n                               original_cost='56', impaired='50', recovered='54', capped_recovery='56')\n\n    liability = Q(5)/Q('1.1') + Q(105)/Q('1.21')\n    equity = 100-liability\n    check('bond_issue_components', (liability, equity) == (Q(11050,121), Q(1050,121)))\n    book, rows = defaultdict(Q), []\n    post(book, rows, 'issue', cash=100, liability=-liability, conversion_equity=-equity)\n    for period in [1, 2]:\n        expense = -book['liability'] * Q(1, 10)\n        post(book, rows, f'interest_{period}', interest_expense=expense, liability=-expense)\n        post(book, rows, f'coupon_{period}', liability=5, cash=-5)\n        check(f'carrying_after_coupon_{period}', -book['liability'] == [Q(1050,11), Q(100)][period-1])\n    check('coupon_and_discount_accretion', book['interest_expense'] == Q(2260,121))\n    redeemed, converted = book.copy(), book.copy()\n    redemption_rows, conversion_rows = list(rows), list(rows)\n    post(redeemed, redemption_rows, 'redemption_at_maturity', liability=100, cash=-100)\n    post(converted, conversion_rows, 'conversion_at_maturity', liability=100, issued_share_equity=-100)\n    check('bond_settlement_paths', redeemed['liability'] == converted['liability'] == 0 and\n          converted['cash'] == 90 and converted['conversion_equity'] == -equity)\n    check('coupon_equals_yield_boundary', Q(5)/Q('1.05')+Q(105)/Q('1.1025') == 100)\n    journals['bond_redemption'], journals['bond_conversion'] = redemption_rows, conversion_rows\n    values['bond'] = dict(issue_liability=str(liability), issue_equity=str(equity),\n                          total_interest_expense=str(book['interest_expense']))\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfor n in ['scripts/core0_ir_v1.py','scripts/context_chronology_v1.py']:\n p=Path(n);print(n);print('\\\\n'.join(l for l in p.read_text().splitlines() if l.startswith(('class ','def ')))[:2300])\np=Path('data/accounting-master/next-plan.md');print('next-plan',p.read_text()[:600])\np=Path('scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text()); seq=d if isinstance(d,list) else d.get('phases',[]);print('P08 catalog',json.dumps(next((x for x in seq if x.get('id')=='P08'),None)))\np=Path('/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/scholarly-literature-audit-policy.md');print('literature policy',p.read_text()[:1900])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\nclass _Failure(Exception):\nclass Diagnostic:\nclass CompileResult:\nclass ValidationResult:\ndef _pairs(value: Mapping[str, Any] | Iterable[tuple[str, Any]] | None) -> tuple[tuple[str, Any], ...]:\ndef _tuple(value: Iterable[Any] | None) -> tuple[Any, ...]:\ndef _fraction(value: Fraction | int | str | Decimal) -> Fraction:\ndef rational(value: Fraction | int | str | Decimal) -> dict[str, str]:\ndef parse_rational(value: Mapping[str, str]) -> Fraction:\ndef _clean_id(value: str) -> str:\ndef _iso(value: str, where: str) -> str:\ndef _string(value: str) -> str:\ndef binding_projection(value: Any) -> Any:\ndef _instant(value: str, where: str) -> str:\ndef _time(kind: str, start: str, end: Optional[str], calendar: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\nclass Expr:\nclass Literal(Expr):\nclass Ref(Expr):\nclass External(Expr):\nclass Call(Expr):\nclass Binary(Expr):\nclass Unary(Expr):\nclass ArrayExpr(Expr):\nclass RecordExpr(Expr):\nclass UseDecl:\nclass SourceDecl:\nclass EntityDecl:\nclass BookDecl:\nclass AccountDecl:\nclass OpeningDecl:\nclass ObservationDecl:\nclass SymbolDecl:\nclass LetDecl:\nclass ConstraintDecl:\nclass ContractDecl:\nclass AlternativeDecl:\nclass ScenarioDecl:\nclass ReportDecl:\nclass UnsupportedDecl:\nclass Program:\nclass ReadingBinding:\nclass OpeningBinding:\nclass ReportBinding:\nclass PackageBinding:\nclass AssumptionBinding:\nclass SymbolAdmission:\nclass AlternativeBinding:\nclass CompileBindings:\ndef _unique(rows, attr, key, code):\ndef _validate_bindings(bindings: CompileBindings) -> None:\ndef _empty_ir() -> dict[str, Any]:\ndef _diag(code: str, message: str, location: str, capability: Optional[str] = None,\nclass _Compiler:\ndef _numeric_type(typ: str) -> bool:\ndef _is_scalar(typ: str) -> bool:\ndef _merge_context(left: Optional[str], right: Optional[str], owner: str, compiler: _Compiler) -> Optional[str]:\ndef _literal_value(expr: Expr, where: str) -> Any:\ndef _arithmetic(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Any:\ndef _compare(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Optional[bool]:\ndef _fold_bool(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Optional[bool]:\ndef compile_program(program: Program, bindings: CompileBindings,\ndef _load_schema() -> dict[str, Any]:\ndef _invalid(code: str, message: str, location: str) -> Diagnostic:\ndef _nodes(ir: Mapping[str, Any]) -> tuple[dict[str, tuple[str, Mapping[str, Any]]],\nscripts/context_chronology_v1.py\nclass P06Error(ValueError):\ndef fail(code: str, message: str, location: str = \"\") -> None:\ndef _fraction(value: Any, where: str = \"value\") -> Fraction:\ndef _iso_date(value: Any, where: str) -> date:\ndef _instant(value: Any, where: str) -> datetime:\nclass Context:\nclass MappingRule:\ndef _context_mismatch(a: Context, b: Context) -> tuple[str, str] | None:\ndef _check_mapping_graph(rules: Sequence[MappingRule]) -> None:\ndef compatible_context(source: Context | Mapping[str, Any], target: Context | Mapping[str, Any],\ndef map_context(source: Context | Mapping[str, Any], target: Context | Mapping[str, Any],\ndef check_partition(population: Iterable[str], members: Mapping[str, Iterable[str]], *,\ndef map_components(source: Context, target: Context, rule: MappingRule, *,\ndef combine_partitions(partitions: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]]) -> dict[str, Any]:\ndef _availability(value: Any, *, timezone_name: str | None, date_only_policy: str | None, where: str) -> datetime:\ndef _validate_assertions(assertions: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]]) -> dict[str, Mapping[str, Any]]:\ndef select_evidence(assertions: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]], cutoff: str | datetime | date, *,\ndef _row_context(row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> str:\ndef subtract_cumulative(total: Mapping[str, Any], earlier: Mapping[str, Any], *,\ndef _validate_joint_law(law: Any, where: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\ndef admit_uncertainty(record: Mapping[str, Any], *, known_records: Mapping[str, Mapping[str, Any]] | None = None,\ndef guard_information_view(view: Mapping[str, Any], *, event_time: str | date, request: str = \"exogenous_stress\") -> dict[str, Any]:\nclass DebtConstituent:\ndef _query_signature(query: Mapping[str, Any]) -> str:\ndef interest_certificate(constituents: Sequence[DebtConstituent], target_rate: Fraction | str | int,\ndef resolve_bullet_debt(constituents: Sequence[DebtConstituent | Mapping[str, Any]], query: Mapping[str, Any], *,\ndef adapt_core_context(row: Mapping[str, Any], *, perimeter_version: str, gross_net: str,\ndef adapt_p03_reading(binding: Any, context: Context, *, historical_byte_vintage: str = \"unknown\") -> dict[str, Any]:\ndef adapt_p01_source(row: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\nclass P06Engine:\nnext-plan # Accounting master — refreshed next plan\n\nUpdated: 2026-10-03T00:55:26.160146+00:00\n\nNext eligible phase: P05.\nMission complete: **no**. Scoped phase acceptance does not close the original gaps.\n\n| Phase | State | Residual work |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| P00 — Verify the accepted baseline | accepted_internal | All G1–G18 retain work; bounded reference checks do not establish accounting or forecast validity. |\n| P01 — Prepare source-context and availability work records | accepted_internal | Publication/version evidence, semantic annotation, incorporated packages and benchmark labels remain open.\nP08 catalog {\"id\": \"P08\", \"kind\": \"worker\", \"name\": \"Resolve authority and corporate-method obligations\", \"deps\": [\"P01\"], \"gaps\": [\"G4\", \"G7\", \"G8\"], \"requirements\": [\"MC06\", \"MC15\", \"MC17\", \"MC19\", \"MC29\", \"MC30\"], \"objective\": \"Prepare dated primary-authority support and implement or precisely specify the next supported corporate/financing operations: revenue, tax, leases, FX, complex groups and bonds. Inspect legitimate primary ASC/ASBE/IFRS-related authority and adopted research; preserve access blocks and jurisdiction limits. Choose a complete internally supportable operation slice and leave the wider queue visible.\", \"deliverables\": [\"authority-and-methods.json\", \"result.md\"], \"criteria\": [\"Claims have inspected primary paragraph/section anchors and jurisdiction/effective-period limits; unavailable texts remain uninspected.\", \"A supported operation slice has preconditions, recognition, measurement, state/posting effects, note links and exact multi-period cases.\", \"Same-fact cross-standard comparisons explain supported differences; source absence is not silently replaced by company practice.\", \"Missing methods and material unresolved interpretations are recorded as specific follow-up work; no professional engagement or paid data.\"], \"test_file\": \"tests/test_accounting_p08.py\", \"output_dir\": \"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P08\"}\nliterature policy # Scholarly Literature Audit Policy\n\nThis policy is intended for research, monograph, survey, and method-design\nwork where agents cite academic literature or decide whether a literature\nreview is complete enough for skeptical scholarly review. It is\nproject-independent. Project-local plans may add stricter rules.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n- Citation counts, journal rankings, and conference rankings are coverage and\n  prioritization signals only. They do not prove correctness, relevance,\n  originality, convergence, empirical validity, or implementation readiness.\n- A literature claim is supported only by checked primary-source technical text:\n  the relevant section, equation, theorem, proof, algorithm, appendix, or\n  experiment must be inspected and cited with enough specificity for a reviewer\n  to find it.\n- Abstracts, titles, metadata snippets, introductions, conclusions, and venue\n  prestige are insufficient for theorem-level or algorithm-level claims.\n- Retractions, withdrawals, expressions of concern, errata, and obvious\n  version conflicts must be checked and recorded before a paper is used as\n  support.\n- A serious literature survey must explain why important omitted papers are\n  omitted. Silence about a famous or recent paper is a reviewer-risk item.\n\n## Required Ledgers\n\nCreate or update separate ledgers when the task is literature-critical:\n\n1. **Source-support ledger.** For each paper: title, authors, year, DOI/arXiv/URL,\n   local artifact path when available, publication status, retraction/quarantine\n   status, full-text status, inspected technical sections, inspected equation,\n   theorem, algorithm, table, and appendix identifiers, and claims allowed or\n   forbidden from that paper.\n2. **Citation and venue metadata ledger.** For each paper when metadata is\n   available: citation count, citation source, access date, venue, venue metric\n   source, access date, an\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"This is a read-only planning phase. The recovery snapshot is accurate: both P08 deliverables and tests/test_accounting_p08.py are absent; neither prior attempt contains a structured plan response.\",\n    \"Choose the issuer lifecycle of a simple compound convertible bond as the bounded operation slice. Revenue, tax, leases, FX and complex groups remain explicit method obligations; this slice cannot close MC06, MC15, MC17, MC19, MC29, MC30 or G4/G7/G8 generally.\",\n    \"Use synthetic facts, exact rational arithmetic, annual coupon periods and an Australian for-profit reporting basis within verified source applicability. AASB adoption is not universal IFRS jurisdiction authority.\",\n    \"Use existing Python and standard-library packages. No model launches, installations, protected-file changes, paid sources or professional engagement are needed.\"\n  ],\n  \"checks\": [\n    \"Before implementation, record the evidence contract and default audit in progress.md: question, existing dossier comparator, source-supported lifecycle acceptance criterion, authority/applicability and journal/state vetoes, explanatory diagnostics, nonclaims and planned artifacts. These are deterministic conformance checks, not a stochastic experiment or forecast comparison.\",\n    \"Run python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p08.py' -v. Tests must exercise the actual parameterized implementation, with independently derived present-value and cash-flow expectations.\",\n    \"Run python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p08.py --check. Require valid schemas, existing source paths, matching retained-byte hashes, resolvable claim/paragraph/note links, applicable editions, reproducible calculations and agreement between generated cases and deliverables.\",\n    \"Test issue, both coupon periods, redemption and maturity conversion; independently reconcile liability roll-forward, cash, interest expense, equity and share count. Test a second principal/rate configuration so hard-coded dossier outputs cannot pass.\",\n    \"Test missing authority, wrong jurisdiction, out-of-period editions, overview-only or company-policy support, unsupported contract features, duplicate/conflicting events, out-of-order accruals, repeated settlement, insufficient cash and failure atomicity.\",\n    \"Verify comparator cases share identical economic inputs. Unsupported standards must return an explicit unresolved result, never inherit another standard's treatment.\",\n    \"Before returning, verify all three required files exist, rerun checks after repairs, enumerate every changed file and compare protected-file hashes. Reserve the final 120 seconds for checks and reporting.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"AGENTS.md\",\n    \"docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\",\n    \"docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\",\n    \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P08/plan-0.recovery.json\",\n    \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P08/plan-0.process.json\",\n    \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/result-review.json\",\n    \"docs/design/research/standards-support.json\",\n    \"docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.pdf\",\n    \"docs/design/research/standards/aasb132.txt\",\n    \"docs/design/review/accounting-dossiers/compound-bond.md\",\n    \"scripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py\",\n    \"scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\",\n    \"scripts/context_chronology_v1.py\",\n    \"docs/design/research/source-support.json\",\n    \"docs/design/research/claim-support.json\"\n  ],\n  \"issues\": [\n    \"The existing compound-bond checker verifies declared arithmetic but does not establish primary authority for subsequent measurement; the dossier explicitly identifies this omission.\",\n    \"The retained authority register reports blocked FASB access and pending official ASBE verification. Company disclosures and unofficial reproductions cannot establish the missing treatments.\",\n    \"No P08 implementation, tests or deliverables currently exist. The stopped planning process does not establish an approved plan or completed work.\"\n  ],\n  \"next_actions\": [\n    \"Review this bounded plan against the four original P08 criteria.\",\n    \"Implement the authority register, bond lifecycle, matched comparisons and tests after plan review; preserve any unsuccessful authority acquisition as explicit unresolved work.\",\n    \"Submit actual files and deterministic results for independent review without claiming whole-gap closure.\"\n  ],\n  \"residuals\": [\n    \"Cross-standard numerical differences remain unverified until applicable primary ASC/ASBE text is inspected. If no supported comparator is obtainable, the comparison criterion remains pending even if the bond implementation passes.\",\n    \"Missing subsequent-measurement authority blocks promotion of the complete bond lifecycle as authority-supported; independent source and method preparation may continue.\",\n    \"Revenue allocation, deferred tax, lease remeasurement, FX translation, complex control/consolidation, early bond repurchase, modification, default and other hybrid features remain later operation work.\",\n    \"Engineering conformance cannot establish professional accounting validity, empirical forecast validity, human acceptance or completion of MC01–MC35/G1–G18.\"\n  ],\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"1. Preserve the recovery baseline. Create progress.md only in the implementation role. Record missing deliverables, relevant input hashes, declared new files and remaining checks. Use new scripts/corporate_financing_v1.py, scripts/check_accounting_p08.py and tests/test_accounting_p08.py; archive additional evidence under docs/design/research/p08-v1/. Do not change existing dossiers, shared engines, frozen corpus, controller or master plan.\",\n    \"2. Record the skeptical audit before implementation. The old dossier is an arithmetic regression comparator, not an accounting oracle; journal balance is necessary but insufficient. Material assumptions are synthetic contract eligibility, comparable yield, annual timing, reporting basis, edition selection and settlement funding. Record each assumption's provenance, failure mode and early check. Source failures veto affected claims, not independent preparation. Failed invariants veto implementation acceptance. This revised scope avoids treating a financing example as the complete corporate package.\",\n    \"3. Build authority-and-methods.json with versioned authority, claim, operation, comparison, research and follow-up records. Every authority record needs issuer, official URL, retrieval timestamp, retained path/hash, edition, jurisdiction/entity scope, effective-period and transition conditions, inspected paragraphs/pages, short supporting excerpts and access status. Distinguish inspected text, retained-but-uninspected text, overview, company practice and inaccessible authority. Resolve exact claims through authority IDs; never infer inspection from file presence.\",\n    \"4. Reinspect AASB 132 classification and conversion provisions and its compilation limits. Acquire and inspect applicable primary AASB 9 recognition, measurement, effective-interest and derecognition provisions before supporting the full lifecycle. Inspect applicable disclosure authority for any claimed mandatory note content. For US GAAP, investigate official FASB convertible-debt guidance, including ASU 2020-06 applicability and exceptions; for ASBE, investigate official Ministry of Finance financial-instrument recognition/measurement and presentation standards. Use bounded legitimate official routes, retaining successful bytes and failed-attempt metadata. Preserve known blocks; do not poll unchanged failed routes or bypass access controls.\",\n    \"5. Implement a narrow parameterized issuer operation engine. Inputs identify entity/book, jurisdiction, reporting periods, currency, contract, proceeds, principal, coupons, comparable yield, conversion shares and authority-backed treatment. Preconditions cover contractual-obligation recognition, qualifying fixed-for-fixed conversion, absence of unsupported settlement clauses, permitted measurement, valid chronology and sufficient cash. Implement atomic issue, accrual, coupon, redemption and maturity-conversion transitions with explicit postings, carrying amount, principal, conversion equity, issued shares and event identity. Reject tax, fees, FX, early conversion, modification, default and embedded-feature cases outside the inspected scope.\",\n    \"6. Produce exact multi-period cases dated within all selected editions. Use issue on 2024-01-01, coupons on 2024-12-31 and 2025-12-31, then alternative maturity settlements. Start with cash/equity 20 to fund redemption; proceeds/principal are 100, annual coupon 5, assumed comparable yield 10%, and conversion delivers ten shares. Independently derive initial liability 11050/121 and conversion equity 1050/121; subsequent liability after coupons is 1050/11 then 100, with total interest 2260/121. Expected ending cash is 10 for redemption and 110 for conversion. Generate journals, period movements and reconciled financing notes from the same state history. Label synthetic funding and yield explicitly.\",\n    \"7. Compare the identical contract under each actually supported standard and period. Hold proceeds, dates, coupons, conversion rights and market assumptions fixed; vary only inspected treatment rules. Explain paragraph-supported differences in initial liability/equity, interest and settlement, or supported agreement. Investigate the US single-liability treatment as a candidate requiring verification, not an assumed result. Leave unavailable cells null with exact missing authority/interpretation. No company-policy substitution or invented difference is permitted.\",\n    \"8. Address adopted research proportionately. Reinspect relevant retained ACTUS event/state/payoff sections for any adopted scheduling mechanism and official implementation where available. If adopting a company-simulation method, inspect its relevant technical, evaluation and appendix material first. Record exact support, transfer limits and source-specific inclusion/defer decisions; do not import behavioral parameters or forecast claims. No broad literature rediscovery is required.\",\n    \"9. Keep six explicit method-queue entries: revenue performance obligations/variable consideration; current/deferred tax and tax bases; lease recognition/options/remeasurement; FX transactions/translation/disposal; group control/acquisition/NCI/elimination/disposal; and remaining bond lifecycle features. Each entry identifies missing authority, proposed operation boundary, unresolved interpretation, next exact case and MC/G links. Write result.md with supported behavior, actual implementation, tests, authority limits, decision table, manifest, changed-file inventory and strongest alternative explanation. Embed check results in the declared deliverables; write no additional supervisor files.\"\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"Plan a source-supported compound-bond lifecycle with exact multi-period cases and matched standards comparisons, while preserving specific authority gaps and the wider corporate-method queue.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"PLAN\"\n}"}}
